From: roc-native-macos engine patch series
Subject: [PATCH 0005] Take the root's answer apart with a match
Upstream: not yet sent
Applies to: roc-signals a13ff70e + 0001 + 0002 + 0003 + 0004, platform/Core.roc

What
  `turn` takes the answer of the root's call apart with `match` instead
  of a destructuring statement, and the rest of the turn moves, unchanged,
  into a function of its own, `fired_turn`, which the `match` calls.
  Nothing else changes: same commands, same turns, same work counters.

Why
  With a `table_view` drawing a table, a turn that wrote a few rows of
  the table still cost its size after patch 0004: about 45 ms at a
  million rows. lldb on a --debug build showed three copies per turn in
  the view site, of columns the size of the table: its pending marks
  (16,000,000 bytes at a million rows, in `mark`), a hole column
  (32,000,000, in `settle`) and the shown column (144,000,000, in
  `settle`). A watchpoint on the marks' refcount showed why: the root's
  pass replaced the view site in the root block's child list
  (`refresh`), and that list was shared, so the replace copied the list
  and the view's captured columns were shared for the whole pass. The
  root instance was shared because `turn` took `(root2, out, tx2)` apart
  with a statement: the compiler keeps the parts of a value taken apart
  that way shared until the function returns (the same behaviour as in
  patch 0004; patches/roc-compiler, destructure-sharing), and `root2` is
  then called for the pass. A `match` moves them.

  The other two `(root3, answer3, tx3) = call(..)` statements in `turn`
  are left as they are: their instance is called again only for a walk of
  local-state layers after the pass, which bench/rows does not take.

Measured (engine ms p50 of a turn that writes 3 rows, reproducer app as
in 0004; before = 0001 to 0004)
                    N=10,000   N=100,000   N=1,000,000
  view   before       0.3         2.9         44.6
  view   after        0.3         0.2          0.1
  bench/rows, tick (3 rows written every 100 ms, a `table_view` over
  every row and a reader of the table), 0001 to 0003 against 0001 to
  0005: 2.7 / 12.0 / 63.0 ms against 0.3 / 0.3 / 0.1 ms.
  The grid bench is unchanged (no table; its smoke's scaling checks pass).

---
--- a/platform/Core.roc
+++ b/platform/Core.roc
@@ -10673,8 +10673,19 @@
